 Stacked on #8002 → #8000 → #7999 → #7998 → main; all hand-offs. Block 05 = the monotone-order class: one formation law for every linear extension of the product order (every rule); rows and columns path chains; the 2×2 corner law with corner independence; no right/down turning staircase is first-order Markov in its site values (proved for every nonconstant positive orbit triple under the declared product-rule monotone law); opposite corner classes give the same finite-rectangle law, with two distinct laws only at the executed 2×3 triples; the snake keeps rows and can lose column chains (column 0 survives on 3×3; on the executed 4×3 no column is a chain). Lens before the primary caught the supervisor's own wrong snake control. Historical checker: FIX FIRST on one forbidden mechanism sentence (false; deleted), nothing refuted in the theorems. Lock released.
 
 Current source review found five further P2 groups, corrected in the canonical note and runner with their disposition in REVIEW_HISTORY.md. Same-session confirmation is pending; this appendix records an open review handoff.
+
+## 2026-09-17 block 34 opened for review (supervisor; continuing "pick up the next in the queue")
+Independent PR against `main` (`9a3ffc8d91`); parent on `main`: block 01. Block 34 = the torus memory time of the sphere formation law (block 26's queue item). Proved for the linearized field on the periodic `L × L` level plane: the modes `φ(k) = (1 + e^{ik₁} + e^{ik₂})/3` with `1 − |φ|² = (4/9)[sin²(k₁/2) + sin²(k₂/2) + sin²((k₁ − k₂)/2)]`; the zero mode random-walks (plane average `σ²t/L²`, `σ² = A(3β)/(3β)`), all other modes stationary; **the memory time `τ_L = 3βL²/A(3β)` exactly** (enclosed: `4879`, `19516`, `78065` levels at `β = 6`, `L = 16, 32, 64`), the proxy decaying exponentially at `A(3β)/(3βL²)` after a transient (the infinite plane: algebraically); the stationary transverse variance bracketed by exact lattice sums, `V_L = 2γ log L + 0.353σ²` executed; the tiny tori checked by exact rational covariance recursions. Executed, not claimed: the nonlinear law's plane-average direction diffuses `1.34, 1.14, 1.06, 1.02` times faster than the zero-mode value at `β = 6, 12, 24, 48` (same at `L = 16, 32`), tracking `1/|m|²` of the stationary magnetization within a few percent — the first quantitative target for "spin-wave theory as a theorem"; the linear model calibrates the estimator to `0.97–1.01`. Records: `RESULTS_block34.md`, `CHECKER_block34_findings.md`, `CLAIM_STATUS_CERTIFICATE_block34.md`, `GOAL_block34.md`; specs with outputs. Campaign PRs open: blocks 12–33 (#8146–#8158, #8168, #8170–#8177), none merged, none commented. Queue after block 34: (1) the tight-sibling lemma (six-axis, `p ≥ 453`); (2) the restricted-tree existence proof (`p ≥ 2921`); (3) spin-wave theory as a theorem for the sphere law, with the `1/|m|²` factor as the target; (4) the infinite-plane loss of memory; (5) a count that is not a union bound.
+
+## 2026-09-17 block 34 opened for review as PR #8178 (supervisor)
+PR #8178 (base `main`, independent). Records: `RESULTS_block34.md`, `CHECKER_block34_findings.md`, `CLAIM_STATUS_CERTIFICATE_block34.md`, `GOAL_block34.md`; specs with outputs. Campaign PRs open: blocks 12–34 (#8146–#8158, #8168, #8170–#8178), none merged, none commented. The day's blocks 32–34 opened as independent PRs; the queue's remaining items are all proofs (two six-axis lemmas, spin-wave theory, the infinite plane, the count).
