+# RESULTS — block 34: the torus memory time of the sphere formation law — the linearized zero mode gives `τ_L = 3βL²/A(3β)` exactly, the other modes are stationary and bracketed, the nonlinear direction diffuses `1/|m|²` faster (2026-09-17)
+
+**Deliverables (branch `physics-loop/admissibility-induced-law-block34-sphere-formation-law-torus-memory-time-zero-mode-rate-and-stationary-modes-20260917`, independent PR against `main` at `9a3ffc8d91`; parent on `main`: block 01):** the note `docs/ADMISSIBILITY_RULE_UNSOLDERED_FORMATION_LAW_TORUS_MEMORY_TIME_ZERO_MODE_RATE_EXACTLY_STATIONARY_MODES_BRACKETED_AND_THE_NONLINEAR_LAW_MEASURED_AGAINST_IT_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-17.md`; the runner `scripts/admissibility_rule_unsoldered_formation_law_torus_memory_time_zero_mode_rate_exactly_stationary_modes_bracketed_nonlinear_law_measured_2026_09_17.py` (16 checks, 6 mutations, exact, half a second); the pinned cache; the controls (`specs/supervisor_control_block34_torus_msd.py`, `..._torus_sim.py`) and the refuting pass (`..._refuter.py`) with outputs; `GOAL_block34.md`; `CHECKER_block34_findings.md`; this record; `CLAIM_STATUS_CERTIFICATE_block34.md`; appends to the shared records.
+
+**Result.**
+- T1 (proved): on the periodic `L × L` level plane the linearized transverse field splits into modes with multiplier `φ(k) = (1 + e^{ik₁} + e^{ik₂})/3`, `1 − |φ|² = (4/9)[sin²(k₁/2) + sin²(k₂/2) + sin²((k₁ − k₂)/2)]`; the zero mode random-walks (plane average `σ²t/L²` per component, `σ² = A(3β)/(3β)`), every other mode is stationary with variance `σ²/(1 − u_k)`.
+- T2 (exact): the rational covariance recursion on the tori `L = 2, 3, 4` equals the mode formula at every level tested.
+- T3 (exact): the memory time `τ_L = 3βL²/A(3β)` enclosed to width `< 1/10` at `β = 6, 12, 24, 48`, `L = 16, 32, 64` (`4879`, `19516`, `78065` at `β = 6`); the proxy decays exponentially at `A(3β)/(3βL²)` after a transient (the infinite plane: algebraically); `V_L ∈ [3/(4π²), 9/16]σ²S_L` with exact lattice sums whose increments are `2π log 2 ± 1`; executed `V_L = 2γ log L + 0.353σ² + o(1)`.
+- Executed (not claimed): the nonlinear law's plane-average direction diffuses with `D₁/(σ²/L²) = 1.34, 1.14, 1.06, 1.02` at `β = 6, 12, 24, 48` (`L = 16`; `1.42, 1.18` at `L = 32`), the same at both sizes within errors, tracking `1/|m|²` of the stationary magnetization within `3–8 %`; the linear model returns `0.97–1.01` under the same estimator; an exponential-fit estimator was found unreliable at the seed counts used and is recorded.
+
+**What this changes.** Block 26's "memory time of order `βL²`" is exact for the linearized field and quantified for the nonlinear law (`≈ |m|² τ_L`); the `1/|m|²` factor is the first quantitative target for "spin-wave theory as a theorem". The infinite-plane loss of memory remains block 26's conjecture.
+
+**Seats.** Supervisor-run: lens (the zero mode isolates the memory time) → controls (block 26's sampler on tori; the exponential-fit estimator rejected on the linear model's own calibration; the mean-squared angular displacement adopted) → contract → primary (T1–T3, runner) → refuting pass (floating-point covariance recursion on `L = 8`; memory times in floating point; an independent rotated-pole sampler; `V_L` by direct summation) → fold (a classical name colliding with a section title in the runner's scan; removed) → census 6/6 in-family → gates → PR.
